# The reverse direction over a real corpus.  googletest-trailing_return_types
# already establishes that the forward pass rebuilds here, so what this adds is
# the second leg: every trailing return type the forward pass produced -- plus
# the ones googletest writes itself -- moved back, and the result rebuilt.
#
# No EXPECT_ROUNDTRIP_IDENTICAL: the guards on the Leading direction are
# strictly tighter than the Trailing ones (a declarator that cannot be
# restructured, a type that resolves in class scope), so a corpus this size is
# expected to keep some declarations in trailing form.  Rebuild and converge
# are the assertions that matter.
REPO=googletest
RULESET=trailing_return_types
RULESET_THEN=leading_return_types
EXPECT=pass
